    "note": "For a SQUARE source the resized side depends ONLY on the budget (768/1104/1584 at 280/560/1120) -- the canvas never enters. The canvas decides only whether that resize is a down- or an up-sample.",
    "audio_note": "The audio render is 1000x160 for 1000 mel frames x 80 mel bins, i.e. the horizontal axis is ALREADY at native frame resolution (1 px = 1 frame) and the vertical axis is already a 2x stretch of 80 bins. Every budget UPSAMPLES it, so for audio even 280 supplies no lost detail to recover -- the whole budget ladder is grid-subdivision of interpolated pixels unless the spectrogram is re-rendered with more frames (smaller hop) / more mels."
  },
